            {
              "id": "1771324794212_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "##Context\nAssume the role of someone who is a skilled Oracle Incentive Compensation plan administrator.\n\n\n##Instructions\nProvide a concise high-level functional summary of the expression named {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.exprname}} with the following syntax {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.exprsyntax}}  that is understandable by a payee with only knowledge of basic mathematics.\n\n##Expression Details from Database\nWhere {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.expressiondetails}} \n\n##Acceptance Criteria\nDo not embellish or include a closing statement.\n\n##Rule Set for Guidance\nReference this set of rules to help you translate the syntax, but do not use them in your response.\n\nOracle Incentive Compensation offers the ability to create custom expressions used in calculating performance and compensation. The expression builder uses common Oracle SQL syntax and SQL functions.    Oracle uses the following dot notation to indicate variables and the retrieved values  <Object>.<Value Name>   The following are the types of predefined Objects that can be found in this dot notation with a description. Definitions of these values will be in the format <Object Name> - <Meaning>  Participant - A person eligible for incentive compensation payments  Plan Component - An object that is used to calculate earnings.  Plan components functionally differ based on the different ways organizations wish to incentivize participants  Measure - Measures also know as performance measures are used to calculate performance or attainment on a specific objective.   Credit - Credit represents a transaction or performance that an individual participant is eligible for payment on.  Values from Credits typically indicate something from the transaction itself that being used for calculation of performance or earnings.  Plan - A plan represents a group of plan components to represent a participants complete list of earnings and how a participant will be compensated.  Rate Table Rate - Is a rate that is retrieved from a predefined rate structure. The value of the Rate Table Rate will vary based on the rate table's structure and the participants performance.  Functions - Are predefined operators that will do certain database tasks, mathematical, or logical operations.       The below are common options available for use in an expression as a Value Name.  Definitions of these values will be in the format <Value Name> - <Meaning>   Values available related to targets include the below. Interval Target - The target for an interval which is a collection of period goals.  Target - The total goal or target for a collection of periods or intervals.  ITD Target - the Interval to Date Target.   Target Incentive - is a amount of compensation associated with a compensation plan that the participant is eligible for. TI Weight - is the weight or percentage of a target incentive that is associated with an individual plan component.    Oracle's expression builder also offers the ability of users to pull results from a custom defined performance measure or plan component for use in calculation.    These are represented as follows in an expression in the format <object name> - <meaning>   Measure result - Performance Measure results  Plan component result - Plan Component Results    When custom defined measures or plan components are used they will be shown in the following dot notations.    Measure result.<Performance Measure Name>.<Value Name>  Plan component result.<Plan Component Name>.<Value Name>    In example if I need results ITD Output Achieved from a performance measure named Revenue the format would be Measure result.Revenue.ITD Output Achieved."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
